1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,377
<i>Chief, excuse me.</i>

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,045
<i>Someone's looking for you downstairs.</i>

3
00:00:04,129 --> 00:00:08,299
<i>Didn't you say you would give me a tour</i>
<i>of your office when you had time?</i>

4
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:10,385
- [JORDAN] <i>It's kinda weird, right?</i>
<i>- Abi.</i>

5
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:14,514
<i>"I'd like to thank someone</i>
<i>very special to me."</i>

6
00:00:14,597 --> 00:00:17,142
<i>"My younger brother, Oliver."</i>

7
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:19,978
<i>Where are your parents?</i>

8
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:21,730
<i>They're dead.</i>

9
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:23,273
<i>They're long gone.</i>

10
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:25,942
[JORDAN]<i> I spoke with the taxi driver</i>
<i>already. He agreed to meet.</i>

11
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,403
[BILLY] <i>Maybe we need to let</i>
<i>the authorities handle this.</i>

12
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:30,321
[JORDAN]
<i>You know that won't achieve anything.</i>

13
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,240
- <i>Caloy! Let him go.</i>
- <i>And your family--</i>

14
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:39,330
You still haven't learned your lesson?

15
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:40,999
Huh? [GRUNTS]

16
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:44,544
- [CALOY SHOUTS]
- [BLOWS LAND]

17
00:00:44,627 --> 00:00:45,503
Is that all you got?

18
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:47,589
[GRUNTS]

19
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:49,716
- [GRUNTS, LAUGHS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

20
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:51,301
[EXCLAIMS]

21
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:53,803
[SPITS]

22
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:56,431
That's what you get
for not minding your business!

23
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:58,725
- [SLAP LANDS]
- [WHIMPERS]

24
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:01,436
- [SOBS] <i>I'm sorry.</i>
<i>- Stay out of it, kid.</i>

25
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:04,272
<i>- This is between your mom and me!</i>
<i>- Stop it!</i>

26
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:06,441
<i>- Huh?!</i>
<i>- Enough! Leave him alone!</i>

27
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,650
<i>- Back off!</i>
- [BODY THUDS]

28
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:10,570
<i>Enough, Daddy! Please!</i>

29
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,280
<i>- Dad! </i>[SOBS]
<i>- Knock it off!</i>

30
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:13,198
<i>- Stay out of it!</i>
<i>- Hey!</i>

31
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:14,574
- [WHIMPERS]
<i>- Stop it!</i>

32
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:16,618
<i>You're hurting him!</i>

33
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:18,912
<i>Let him go!</i>

34
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:20,080
[SLAPS]

35
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:23,792
<i>- Enough!</i>
- [JADE SHOUTS]

36
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:26,586
[CALOY GRUNTS]

37
00:01:26,669 --> 00:01:28,630
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [JORDAN GRUNTS]

38
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:29,964
[SHOUTS]

39
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:34,928
[KICKS, BLOWS LANDING]

40
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,554
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

41
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,016
- [KICK LANDS]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

42
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:43,102
[BOTH GRUNTING]

43
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:46,898
[KICKS, BLOW LAND]

44
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:48,316
[WOMAN SCREAMS]

45
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:49,859
Oh my goodness!

46
00:01:50,902 --> 00:01:54,531
- [PEOPLE MURMURING] Poor guy.
- [GRUNTS LOUDLY]

47
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,286
Who's your boss?

48
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:02,539
Who was that woman?

49
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:04,582
- What woman?
- Tell me!

50
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:06,835
I don't know what you're talking about!
I swear!

51
00:02:06,918 --> 00:02:08,586
- Tell me!
- I have nothing to tell you!

52
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:11,589
Tell me, Caloy.

53
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,049
I have nothing to say!

54
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,592
Who was that woman?!

55
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:17,303
Help me!

56
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:19,472
Please, help me!

57
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:23,434
- Help! Please! Please, help me!
- Hey!

58
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:24,519
[JORDAN] Let me go!

59
00:02:24,602 --> 00:02:27,021
He's the criminal! Not me!

60
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,940
- Please, help me.
- Caloy!

61
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:31,776
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

62
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:38,575
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:16,696
Auntie Pres.

64
00:03:16,779 --> 00:03:18,156
- Billy.
- Oliver.

65
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:19,532
- Billy…
- Are you okay?

66
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:20,992
- Billy.
- What happened?

67
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:23,870
I'm fine. I just got into a fight.

68
00:03:24,621 --> 00:03:27,874
I told him that
he should've told his teacher.

69
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:30,335
There was no teacher around then.

70
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:34,213
Oliver, what happened?

71
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,132
Who started it?

72
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:37,217
He did.

73
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:41,512
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:43,306
He punched me first!

75
00:03:43,389 --> 00:03:45,016
That's not true!

76
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:47,393
This kid is such a liar!

77
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:50,772
- Excuse me. Please don't call him a liar.
- Why shouldn't we?

78
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:54,567
You better not expect our son
to apologize for what happened!

79
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:57,362
Look at the poor thing!

80
00:03:57,445 --> 00:03:59,447
Where are his parents?!

81
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,783
[PRECIOUS] I am his legal guardian.

82
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:05,662
Auntie Precious and I
are Oliver's legal guardians.

83
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,747
And my brother is not a liar.

84
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:11,751
We told him to stay away from trouble
as much as possible.

85
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:16,047
But we also taught him
to fight back when necessary.

86
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:20,343
Ah, so you're the one
who taught this kid to be violent?

87
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:23,930
Again, as long as it's self-defense.

88
00:04:24,013 --> 00:04:26,683
So you're perfectly fine
with Oliver punching our son?

89
00:04:26,766 --> 00:04:28,226
- Yes!
- Of course not.

90
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:29,310
Huh?

91
00:04:29,894 --> 00:04:33,189
No wonder your brother is a delinquent.

92
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:35,566
You're tolerating his bad behavior!

93
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:36,901
What a shameless family!

94
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:43,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

95
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:47,537
- [BILLY GRUNTS]
- [GASPING]

96
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:51,082
You should be ashamed!

97
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:55,670
A kid defending himself
doesn't make him a delinquent.

98
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:57,797
Dr. Ronquillo,

99
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:02,969
can we call this kid's real parents?

100
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:04,762
I don't want to talk to these people!

101
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:08,933
They're both gone,
so you'll have to deal with us.

102
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:11,644
Folks, let's all act like adults.

103
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:15,898
Someone will be joining us
to tell us what really happened.

104
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:16,941
[DOOR OPENS]

105
00:05:17,525 --> 00:05:22,280
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

106
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:25,867
I asked them to join us so we can
hear Suzie's side of the story.

107
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:30,997
Suzie, who really started the fight?

108
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:35,710
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

109
00:05:36,335 --> 00:05:37,670
Thank you again.

110
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,589
Sir Edgar, thank you.

111
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:41,382
Thank you for coming.

112
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:45,762
We just did the right thing
by telling the truth.

113
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:48,473
Thank you for protecting our baby.

114
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:50,641
Thank you for the cupcakes as well.

115
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,810
Biboy is really a bully.

116
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:54,395
He won't stop.

117
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:56,397
You don't have to worry about him, Suzie.

118
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:59,108
Aren't you scared of him?

119
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,651
Him and his entire group?

120
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:03,571
Nope. I'm not backing down from them.

121
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:05,239
I'm brave like my big sister.

122
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:07,075
- Mm…
- Very good.

123
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:09,577
You two are like peas in a pod.

124
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:12,747
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

125
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:18,628
[BUSY TONE]

126
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:21,923
- [UTENSILS CLINK]
- Fork here.

127
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:24,509
How do you feel? Does it still hurt?

128
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,344
No, Billy. It's just a small bruise.

129
00:06:26,427 --> 00:06:28,137
- No, Oliver.
- Put some ice on it.

130
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:33,476
That small bruise of yours
will take time to heal.

131
00:06:33,559 --> 00:06:35,561
But it'll still heal, right?

132
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:36,479
[MOUTHS] No!

133
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:40,191
I'm sorry, Auntie.

134
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:41,484
I'm sorry too, Billy.

135
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:43,277
I know you guys are busy.

136
00:06:43,361 --> 00:06:45,363
I'm sorry for being a burden.

137
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:48,241
What? Don't say that, Oliver.

138
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:51,410
You're never going to be a burden.

139
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:54,455
- You're our baby boy!
- No!

140
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,374
Tsk, I'm not a baby anymore!

141
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:58,126
Stop calling me that!

142
00:06:58,209 --> 00:07:01,045
Okay, fine. You're not
our baby boy anymore,

143
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:02,630
but you will never be a burden to us.

144
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:06,008
Auntie Pres and I
will always have your back.

145
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:07,510
Me too, Billy.

146
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:10,263
That's why I'm bulking up. See?

147
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:11,889
- Look at those biceps!
- Cut that out.

148
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:13,599
You already punched someone.

149
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,435
Violence is never the answer, Oliver!

150
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:17,645
I know, Auntie.

151
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:20,982
But all I'm saying is,
if anyone hurts Billy?

152
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:23,734
- I'll knock them out.
- Unbelievable.

153
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:26,487
- You don't listen, do you?
- Just like Billy.

154
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:29,449
Don't blame me.

155
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:31,617
- Put some ice on that.
- Listen to me, Billy.

156
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:34,620
Stop tolerating Oliver's behavior.

157
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:36,456
- It is wrong and unacceptable.
- [BILLY] But--

158
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:37,707
- Hear me out--
- No, no, no.

159
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:41,961
No buts, no hear-me-outs. None of that.

160
00:07:42,044 --> 00:07:45,006
Violence is wrong.

161
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:47,592
It doesn't matter who started it,

162
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:49,844
the bottom line is, no fighting.

163
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:51,053
[OLIVER] Uh-oh.

164
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:53,973
Okay, Auntie Pres. Calm down.

165
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:56,017
- Chill out, Auntie.
- I'm worried about you two.

166
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:58,769
- Yes, we know.
- Let's hug it out.

167
00:07:58,853 --> 00:08:00,480
- Come on!
- Chill, okay?

168
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:02,398
- Chill? Whatever! Let's eat.
- [BOTH EXCLAIM]

169
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:03,941
No violence, remember?

170
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,151
- That's wrong.
- Yes.

171
00:08:05,234 --> 00:08:06,277
- No to violence.
- Oh, really?

172
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:08,237
- [EXCLAIMS] Get him!
- [OLIVER SHOUTS]

173
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:11,908
- I am not a criminal.
- Nope.

174
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:13,242
He is.

175
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:14,410
Check his record.

176
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,620
[OFFICER] We already have.

177
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:18,164
According to his record,
it was an act of self-defense.

178
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:19,165
Bull!

179
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:20,750
Chief, ask the people who were there.

180
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,335
They'll tell you the truth.

181
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:24,045
They witnessed it!

182
00:08:24,128 --> 00:08:25,796
You think you're the victim here?

183
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:26,923
A lot of people can testify!

184
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:29,133
You were caught on video
trying to stab me!

185
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:31,010
I wasn't looking for trouble!

186
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:33,137
- You attacked me!
- That's not true.

187
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:34,388
Don't believe him! He's a hacker!

188
00:08:34,472 --> 00:08:35,556
- Chief…
- He's an online troll!

189
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,141
- What?!
- And a big fat liar!

190
00:08:37,225 --> 00:08:38,935
- Wait…
- Look, I'm injured!

191
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:41,687
Sir, he's been harassing me and my friend.

192
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:43,105
We had him arrested before.

193
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:45,191
- You should go to jail!
- [ROBBIE] What the hell?

194
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:46,400
- What did you say?!
- Hey!

195
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:48,069
- See?! See?!
- Stop it!

196
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:49,570
Cuff him!

197
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:51,739
- Arrest him!
- This is going online!

198
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:53,241
- Stop that!
- Don't record this!

199
00:08:53,324 --> 00:08:54,242
[OFFICER] Enough.

200
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:55,785
Lock him up already, chief!

201
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:58,496
Boss, are you all right? Boss?

202
00:08:58,579 --> 00:09:00,164
- [JORDAN GRUNTS]
- Boss.

203
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:04,043
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:08,798
[CAMERAS CLICKING]

205
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:13,636
ARM DAY FOR ME! NO SWEAT, NO GAIN.

206
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:17,056
Oh…

207
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:19,642
- Someone's happy.
- Hmm?

208
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:21,602
Is that why you're smiling, Auntie Pres?

209
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:24,981
- Because of Brandon?
- Mm.

210
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:28,150
He's not just charitable.
He's also athletic.

211
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:29,569
- Mm-hmm.
- Watch out, Auntie Pres.

212
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:30,820
He must throw a mean punch too.

213
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:32,989
Boxing's just one of his hobbies.

214
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:34,782
You're defending him!

215
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:38,119
No, I'm just reading
what's listed on his profile.

216
00:09:38,202 --> 00:09:40,162
- Don't be silly.
- Are you two talking?

217
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:42,790
Huh? It's too soon.

218
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:44,083
Okay, Auntie Pres.

219
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:47,420
If you're scared or unsure,

220
00:09:47,503 --> 00:09:49,880
use the LoveSpeak feature.

221
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:50,798
Mm.

222
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:54,385
Ask if anyone knows Brandon.

223
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:58,097
Their feedback can help you
get to know him.

224
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,558
Maybe next time. I'm busy.

225
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,226
With what?

226
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:05,313
With the sanctuary,

227
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:08,024
with Oliver, and even here at home.

228
00:10:08,107 --> 00:10:09,483
And you too.

229
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,943
We're okay.

230
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,069
We're fine!

231
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:14,405
Your baby boy is all grown up

232
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:15,698
and won't even let you hug him.

233
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:16,949
Hmph!

234
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,327
It's your turn.

235
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,661
Huh?

236
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,038
Why are we talking about me now?

237
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:25,750
Why don't you
put yourself first this time?

238
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:27,418
I'm trying!

239
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:31,589
Is it my fault no one passes
my very long checklist?

240
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:34,258
Passing that checklist of yours
is an impossible task.

241
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:38,596
Besides, your life
revolves around home and work.

242
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,139
It's always home, work, home, work.

243
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:42,350
How will you meet someone
who ticks all the boxes?

244
00:10:42,433 --> 00:10:44,393
Listen, Billy.

245
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:48,564
You've been working hard
since you were a kid.

246
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:50,316
- Mm-hmm.
- Am I right?

247
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:53,819
Even after I told you countless times,
"Billy, I got this."

248
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:56,280
You refuse to slow down.

249
00:10:56,364 --> 00:11:00,785
You'd put Biboy's father to shame

250
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:04,789
if he found out all the sacrifices
you made for Oliver.

251
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,165
For all of us.

252
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:09,752
He was asking for
Oliver's parents, wasn't he?

253
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:15,049
Well, he should know that you are
basically Oliver's mom and dad.

254
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:18,719
You sacrificed your childhood
to raise him.

255
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:19,970
You didn't get to have fun.

256
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,263
- Huh?
- [PHONE RINGING]

257
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,599
And who says I'm not having fun?

258
00:11:23,682 --> 00:11:24,767
Mm-hmm.

259
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:26,644
Hello?

260
00:11:26,727 --> 00:11:27,686
Yes, Rain?

261
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,232
Huh?

262
00:11:32,149 --> 00:11:34,527
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:35,945
What happened?

264
00:11:36,028 --> 00:11:37,405
- Jordan!
- Ma'am.

265
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,490
- Boss, I'm his friend.
- Go ahead.

266
00:11:39,573 --> 00:11:40,991
What the hell?

267
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,576
I told you guys not to tell her!

268
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:46,205
I was going to fix this myself.

269
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:48,207
Rain called her.

270
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:50,876
- Wow, traitor.
- You did.

271
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,461
How's Oliver?

272
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:54,880
Oliver is fine, but you're not.

273
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:57,174
- You are so stubborn!
- Ow!

274
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:59,468
I just wanted to talk to the taxi driver.

275
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:00,970
I know the whole story.

276
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:02,346
Okay.

277
00:12:04,765 --> 00:12:06,725
But on the bright side…

278
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:07,893
Jordan, stop.

279
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:12,481
No, really. Look,
Caloy filed a case against me.

280
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:16,944
I'll file a case against him too.

281
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,447
So that means…

282
00:12:20,614 --> 00:12:21,782
A legal battle.

283
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:23,284
Yes.

284
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:28,914
We'll be able to dig up info on Caloy.

285
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:34,044
Maybe we'll find clues or evidence

286
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:35,463
that'll lead us to his employer.

287
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:38,841
And how will you do that
if you're in jail?

288
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:41,677
Everything will be okay.

289
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,220
Boss.

290
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:45,431
Physical assault, grave threats,

291
00:12:45,514 --> 00:12:48,767
and they added possession
of a deadly weapon.

292
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:50,519
That's a hefty bail.

293
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:54,315
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

294
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:55,524
I can handle it.

295
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:58,777
But the problem is,
we just paid the rent for the bar.

296
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:01,363
And didn't you just cash out
for your grandfather's…

297
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:02,740
Rain! Shh!

298
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:05,618
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

299
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:08,120
Look, dude…

300
00:13:09,246 --> 00:13:10,372
I'm sorry.

301
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:12,833
You know, honestly,

302
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:15,002
I really want to smack you right now.

303
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,130
But I'll save that for when you get out.

304
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,342
Let's figure something out.

305
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:24,470
Look, I can handle the bail.

306
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:27,765
I don't think it's that much.

307
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:29,975
Yeah, boss, but…

308
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:32,520
we're still waiting for the person
who has to sign your release.

309
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:33,938
So I think

310
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:36,023
stay.

311
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:37,274
Stay.

312
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:44,949
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

313
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:49,453
Guys, go home.

314
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:52,831
I'll be okay.

315
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,296
- Ma'am, thank you.
- Thank you!

316
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:02,258
You're welcome!
There's more if you want a second round.

317
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:03,509
Go ahead. Eat up.

318
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:08,264
Boss, where did you live
before you went to prison?

319
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:11,392
Hmm. You've gone viral now.

320
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:13,227
LOVELIST'S JORDAN VALENTIN
INVOLVED IN ASSAULT.

321
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:14,728
I don't want to see it.

322
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,196
I'm sorry.

323
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,656
Are you okay?

324
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:27,491
I just want to know the truth.

325
00:14:28,158 --> 00:14:30,369
But not like this.

326
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:34,039
Not this way.

327
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,960
What happened to you?

328
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:39,837
Why did you suddenly snap?

329
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:43,424
You're not like this.

330
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,093
[JADE SCREAMING]

331
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:48,596
[GASPING]

332
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:51,765
[JADE CHOKING]

333
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:53,434
[THUDS]

334
00:14:53,517 --> 00:14:55,269
[DINO GRUNTS]

335
00:14:57,438 --> 00:14:59,481
[JUDE] <i>Get out before I kill you!</i>

336
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:00,649
<i>Get out!</i>

337
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,151
[GROANING]

338
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:05,404
[DINO PANTING]

339
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:07,031
<i>I'm not afraid of you, old man.</i>

340
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:09,450
<i>What about the police? Still not afraid?</i>

341
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,161
<i>I know all the dirty things you've done.</i>

342
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,247
<i>I'll have you arrested for dealing drugs</i>

343
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:18,250
<i>and for abusing my daughter and grandson.</i>

344
00:15:20,044 --> 00:15:21,378
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Daddy.</i>

345
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:27,927
[YOUNG JORDAN CRYING]

346
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:31,597
You're right.

347
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:33,349
I snapped.

348
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:36,769
I was reminded of my dad.

349
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:40,981
You know what happened to Mama.

350
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:45,569
Back then,

351
00:15:47,071 --> 00:15:49,031
I couldn't protect her from Dad.

352
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:53,953
But now, things are different.

353
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:56,246
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:57,748
I'll do whatever it takes

355
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,709
to protect all of us
from people like my dad.

356
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:02,878
People like Caloy.

357
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,464
It's just,

358
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:08,050
I shouldn't have lost control.

359
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:11,220
I shouldn't have let it go this far.

360
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:12,388
[BILLY] Mm-hmm.

361
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:13,764
So, dude, I'm sorry.

362
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:15,015
You don't have to apologize.

363
00:16:17,309 --> 00:16:19,687
You only did that for…

364
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:20,854
For us.

365
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,314
- Aww!
- [GIGGLING]

366
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,899
- Kiss her!
- Kiss!

367
00:16:28,362 --> 00:16:30,447
- Uh, it's all settled.
- Hey, Ralph.

368
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:32,157
Everything's taken care of, Billy.

369
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:33,534
I called Ralph.

370
00:16:33,617 --> 00:16:35,494
Did you guys forget? His dad is a judge.

371
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:37,538
- Mm-hmm.
- Ralph, thank you.

372
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:39,081
Dad took care of it, bro.

373
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:40,874
He personally called the judge on duty,

374
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:42,876
so your release was signed right away.

375
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,962
- Thank you.
- Ralph, thank you.

376
00:16:45,504 --> 00:16:47,089
Dude! Hey.

377
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:48,632
- Thank you!
- [MAN 1] Kiss!

378
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:50,634
- Come on, just one!
- Just one kiss!

379
00:16:50,718 --> 00:16:53,012
- [JORDAN] You two kiss!
- [MAN 1] Kiss!

380
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:56,432
[CHEERING]

381
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:58,517
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

382
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,686
- [YANI] Cheers!
- To…

383
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:01,687
Freedom.

384
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,565
- To freedom!
- To freedom!

385
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:06,025
[JORDAN] To freedom.

386
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:07,234
- Cheers.
- [BOTTLE CLINKS]

387
00:17:08,652 --> 00:17:09,695
- Ralph.
- Hmm?

388
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:12,781
Thanks again. You're a real lifesaver.

389
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,534
I got you, brother.

390
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:19,830
Your boyfriend's family really does have
some serious influence, Charm.

391
00:17:19,913 --> 00:17:21,165
[CHARM] Oh!

392
00:17:21,248 --> 00:17:22,958
That's my Ralph!

393
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:24,877
- Aw!
- Aw!

394
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,463
- Well, he's a nepo kid.
- [TONI] Hey, come on.

395
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:29,506
I'm just kidding. Don't be so sensitive!

396
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:31,383
- To freedom!
- To freedom!

397
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:33,635
- Cheers!
- Freedom, freedom, freedom!

398
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:36,055
- I'm just kidding!
- He's just kidding.

399
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:37,347
[BOTTLES CLINKING]

400
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:39,725
Oh, speaking of freedom,

401
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:41,185
what about LoveList?

402
00:17:41,268 --> 00:17:44,813
When are we finally going to be free
of that Caloy?

403
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:45,939
Hmm.

404
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:50,027
[MARJ] Guys, this is really worrying,
especially now.

405
00:17:50,903 --> 00:17:54,865
Just when LoveLine started bringing
our members back too.

406
00:17:54,948 --> 00:17:56,200
Check your socials.

407
00:17:57,367 --> 00:17:59,369
The haters have multiplied too.

408
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:00,871
I know.

409
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:02,873
I'll make a post.

410
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:05,501
I'll explain everything.

411
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:06,794
No, no. No need.

412
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:10,172
The best thing to do is…

413
00:18:10,255 --> 00:18:11,632
No reaction?

414
00:18:11,715 --> 00:18:16,220
Is to think of ways
to improve LoveList's services even more.

415
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:19,681
And keep promoting our advocacy.

416
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:22,101
- We can do this.
- Okay.

417
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:23,894
Cheers. We can do this.

418
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:26,980
- [YANI] Cheers!
- I'm just going to the restroom.

419
00:18:27,064 --> 00:18:29,525
- [TONI] That's what she said.
- Excuse me.

420
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:33,904
[CHARM] But seriously, once I find out
who Caloy's accomplice is…

421
00:18:33,987 --> 00:18:37,908
- [CHARM] I swear! I swear!
- [TONI] Yes, girl, stay mad.

422
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:42,204
- [TONI] Love, come on.
- [YANI] I'm kidding, you guys.

423
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:44,331
- [YANI] Come on, cheers again!
- [JORDAN CLEARS THROAT]

424
00:18:44,414 --> 00:18:45,499
[FRIENDS] Cheers!

425
00:18:45,582 --> 00:18:48,585
[TONI] You're such a clown.
Go use the restroom already.

426
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,504
All right, that's enough.

427
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:53,841
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:55,926
- Hmm?
- Sorry.

429
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:57,636
No, it's okay.

430
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:02,015
What's done is done.
There's nothing we can do now.

431
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,059
Let's move on.

432
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:07,020
You have good intentions.

433
00:19:07,980 --> 00:19:09,189
Are you sure?

434
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:13,318
At least this time,
you didn't get stabbed.

435
00:19:14,194 --> 00:19:15,362
You only got punched.

436
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:18,031
[GIGGLING]

437
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:21,118
Thanks, dude.

438
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,452
Thank you.

439
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:26,957
But you know what
I've been thinking about?

440
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:30,169
How did Caloy get there before us?

441
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:34,298
How did he know you were
going to meet the taxi driver?

442
00:19:35,632 --> 00:19:37,467
<i>I think he'll cooperate.</i>

443
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:40,304
<i>If not, I'll make him.</i>

444
00:19:40,387 --> 00:19:42,598
<i>What if he's working with Caloy?</i>

445
00:19:42,681 --> 00:19:46,059
<i>This taxi driver</i>
<i>is our best shot right now.</i>

446
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:50,439
He's our only lead to the woman
who gave him the money.

447
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:53,609
<i>Whoever she is,</i>
<i>I won't let her ruin LoveList.</i>

448
00:19:53,692 --> 00:19:57,029
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

449
00:19:57,112 --> 00:19:58,030
<i>You guys are leaving?</i>

450
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:00,199
I don't want to believe it's Val.

451
00:20:00,282 --> 00:20:01,366
Jordan?

452
00:20:02,117 --> 00:20:03,660
Have you guys seen Jordan?

453
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:05,537
Jordan!

454
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:06,914
Hi! Hi!

455
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:09,416
Are you okay?

456
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:10,709
Are you okay? What happened?

457
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:11,752
I'm fine, really.

458
00:20:11,835 --> 00:20:13,754
Tell me everything.

459
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:15,172
I'm good.

460
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:19,468
Val.

461
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,303
Beer?

462
00:20:21,386 --> 00:20:22,387
Can you pass it over?

463
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:24,348
- Pass it over, please.
- Just pass it over.

464
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:26,642
Thanks.

465
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:37,194
You know, Jordan,
you really haven't changed.

466
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:39,863
Guys, back when Jordan and I
were together,

467
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:42,824
every time someone messed with me,
he'd go after them.

468
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:45,744
You really need to watch your temper.

469
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:49,414
But are you okay now?
Did you break any bones?

470
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:51,291
- When's your next follow-up…
- Val.

471
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:52,751
I'm okay.

472
00:20:52,834 --> 00:20:54,336
- Okay.
- Thank you.

473
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,672
Just let me know.

474
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:00,217
Is this awkward?

475
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,551
Sorry.

476
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:03,804
I'm just worried about Jordan.

477
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:08,308
I mean, I know we're not
together anymore, but

478
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:11,645
that doesn't mean I should stop
caring about him, right?

479
00:21:11,728 --> 00:21:15,274
I mean, we're friends.
We have history.

480
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:17,484
- Right?
- Right.

481
00:21:19,152 --> 00:21:20,070
Friends.

482
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:22,364
Real friends don't snitch.

483
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,366
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

484
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:27,744
[MARJ] And someone tipped Caloy off

485
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:30,914
about Jordan's plan to
talk to the taxi driver.

486
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:32,582
So what are you trying to say?

487
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:34,376
Why don't you just say it to my face?

488
00:21:34,459 --> 00:21:37,754
Well, I think you're the snitch.

489
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,215
- [BILLY] Marj.
- Oh my gosh.

490
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:41,717
Stop.

491
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:43,719
We can't just make assumptions, okay?

492
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:45,637
Chief, I'm sorry.

493
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:50,475
It's just that if Valerie
really has nothing to hide,

494
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:54,688
I dare you to show
your messages and calls.

495
00:21:54,771 --> 00:21:56,023
[CHARM] That's right.

496
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:58,066
So we can finally know the truth, right?

497
00:21:58,150 --> 00:21:59,318
- Exactly.
- Exactly.

498
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:01,570
Hey, let's not do this.

499
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:05,490
Jordan, what was
the taxi driver's number again?

500
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:08,076
Let's see if it's in Valerie's phone.

501
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:13,165
Don't you want to know
if she's involved too?

502
00:22:14,791 --> 00:22:16,710
So I'm still the suspect?

503
00:22:16,793 --> 00:22:18,003
- No.
- [CHARM] You know what?

504
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:20,839
Just show us your phone
so we can end this, okay?

505
00:22:20,922 --> 00:22:21,923
No!

506
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:24,217
See? Guilty.

507
00:22:25,552 --> 00:22:27,012
- [MARJ SCOFFS]
- Hey!

508
00:22:27,095 --> 00:22:28,346
- Give me my phone!
- Guys!

509
00:22:28,430 --> 00:22:29,848
- Marj!
- Give it back to me!

510
00:22:29,931 --> 00:22:31,349
- Show it!
- That's enough!

511
00:22:31,433 --> 00:22:33,310
- Give it back! I'll show it!
- Val, just let her.

512
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:35,937
Come on, let's get this over with.
Just let them.

513
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:38,815
So you can prove to them that
you had nothing to do with this.

514
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:40,275
Go ahead.

515
00:22:40,358 --> 00:22:41,610
Them?

516
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:42,736
[SCOFFS]

517
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:45,197
Aren't you suspicious of me too?

518
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:46,990
So what? You're on my side now?

519
00:22:48,366 --> 00:22:51,703
[MARJ] You know, Val,
for the longest time,

520
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:54,164
Chief Billy was the only one
who kept defending you

521
00:22:54,247 --> 00:22:57,417
when we thought you were involved
with that Caloy guy.

522
00:22:57,501 --> 00:23:00,212
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

523
00:23:00,295 --> 00:23:01,171
Fine.

524
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:04,132
No.

525
00:23:04,841 --> 00:23:07,010
What if you delete the evidence first?

526
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:09,971
- No.
- I'll check it myself.

527
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:12,557
I'll do it. Give me your password.

528
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:17,187
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

529
00:23:23,193 --> 00:23:25,445
[GROANS]

530
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:26,363
[ABI] Caloy!

531
00:23:28,406 --> 00:23:30,283
- Oh.
- What are you doing here?

532
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:32,744
Why did you come straight here?
What if someone followed you?

533
00:23:34,412 --> 00:23:35,831
You know, 'Bi…

534
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:38,917
I'd never put you in danger.

535
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:47,884
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

536
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:50,846
Did Jordan really think…

537
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:52,139
[CHUCKLES]

538
00:23:52,222 --> 00:23:53,598
he could outsmart me of all people?

539
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:56,017
Ah, it hurts.

540
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:58,645
That's because you weren't careful.

541
00:23:58,728 --> 00:24:00,689
Wasn't it you who told me

542
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:04,109
to scare that driver?

543
00:24:05,402 --> 00:24:06,278
[BILLY] <i>Okay.</i>

544
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:10,282
<i>How can you be sure</i>
<i>the taxi driver is telling the truth?</i>

545
00:24:10,365 --> 00:24:12,534
<i>I think he'll cooperate.</i>

546
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:15,162
<i>If not, I'll make him.</i>

547
00:24:16,204 --> 00:24:18,081
<i>What if he's working with Caloy?</i>

548
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:22,794
<i>Billy, this taxi driver</i>
<i>is our best shot right now.</i>

549
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:27,549
<i>He's our only lead to the woman</i>
<i>who gave him the money.</i>

550
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:31,595
<i>Whoever she is,</i>
<i>I won't let her ruin LoveList.</i>

551
00:24:31,678 --> 00:24:33,597
<i>I won't let her do that to us.</i>

552
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:35,015
<i>To you.</i>

553
00:24:37,601 --> 00:24:40,854
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

554
00:24:43,273 --> 00:24:44,774
<i>Are you really okay?</i>

555
00:24:44,858 --> 00:24:45,817
<i>There you go again.</i>

556
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:48,069
<i>You're making my problems</i>
<i>your responsibility.</i>

557
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:50,238
<i>- Is it your dad?</i>
<i>- Why do you keep asking me that?</i>

558
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:51,406
<i>You're like a broken record.</i>

559
00:24:51,489 --> 00:24:52,866
<i>Things can't always be this way.</i>

560
00:24:52,949 --> 00:24:56,536
<i>Not now that I'm finally</i>
<i>getting close to my idol.</i>

561
00:24:56,620 --> 00:24:59,122
<i>- Anything for you, Bea.</i>
<i>- What did you say?!</i>

562
00:24:59,206 --> 00:25:00,957
<i>Okay, give me my phone back.</i>

563
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:02,709
<i>- What's this?</i>
<i>- Let me explain.</i>

564
00:25:02,792 --> 00:25:04,127
- [SLAMS]
<i>- Oh!</i>

565
00:25:04,878 --> 00:25:06,463
<i>You witch!</i>

566
00:25:07,088 --> 00:25:08,632
<i>Benilda? Sweetie?</i>
